e_following_comma\",\n+      \"intent\": \"A paired backslash emits one literal backslash; the subsequent outside comma remains a separator, and a paired final backslash is valid.\",\n+      \"input\": \"A\\\\\\\\,B,C\\\\\\\\\",\n+      \"expected\": [\"a\\\\\", \"b\", \"c\\\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"escaped_quotes_do_not_toggle_mode\",\n+      \"intent\": \"Literal escaped quotes outside quotes leave commas active; an escaped quote inside quotes leaves a following comma protected until the closing quote.\",\n+      \"input\": \"A\\\\\\\",B,\\\"C\\\\\\\",D\\\",E\",\n+      \"expected\": [\"a\\\"\", \"b\", \"c\\\",d\", \"e\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"trailing_escape_after_valid_labels\",\n+      \"intent\": \"A trailing unpaired escape outside quotes invalidates the whole input after valid and duplicate labels.\",\n+      \"input\": \"OK,ok,NEXT,TAIL\\\\\",\n+      \"expected\": null\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"trailing_escape_inside_quote_after_valid_label\",\n+      \"intent\": \"An unpaired final backslash inside quoted mode invalidates the whole input despite an earlier valid label.\",\n+      \"input\": \"OK,\\\"TAIL\\\\\",\n+      \"expected\": null\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"unclosed_quote_after_valid_labels\",\n+      \"intent\": \"Opening a quote mid-label without closing it invalidates the whole input even when earlier labels are valid and a comma appears inside the open quote.\",\n+      \"input\": \"OK,NEXT,TAIL\\\"OPEN,STILL OPEN\",\n+      \"expected\": null\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"escaped_final_quote_does_not_close_quote\",\n+      \"intent\": \"A final escaped quote is literal and cannot close quoted mode, so the whole input raises after an earlier valid label.\",\n+      \"input\": \"OK,\\\"TAIL\\\\\\\"\",\n+      \"expected\": null\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"properties\": [\"unique_nonempty_labels\", \"ascii_lowercase\"],\n+  \"rationale\": \"These 23 deterministic ASCII cases cover all ten rules and their interactions: repeated outside separators, quote concatenation and empty quotes, literal commas inside quotes, one-character escapes in both modes, each of the six ordinary and protected whitespace characters, boundary trimming before internal run collapse, protected whitespace breaking runs and surviving alone, ASCII lowercasing regardless of protection, literal punctuation, exact-result deduplication with stable order, empty input, and whole-input errors after valid labels. Expected strings distinguish ordinary collapsed spaces from exact protected characters and multiplicity. Null expectations cover trailing escapes both outside and inside quotes, a quote opened mid-label, and an escaped final quote that leaves quoted mode open. Unicode and non-string inputs are excluded.\"\n+}\n",
